      "line": 432,
      "text": "\\subsection{Global Kuranishi charts} In~\\cite{AMS21}, the authors achieved a breakthrough by constructing a particularly simple representation for the moduli spaces of stable maps in genus $0$: that of a global Kuranishi chart. In~\\cite{HS22} and independently~\\cite{AMS23}, global Kuranishi charts were constructed for moduli spaces of stable maps of arbitrary genus. These constructions allow for a straightforward definition of a virtual fundamental class."
    },
